1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
I reached out to the author Terry Bisson, who said yes. It's read for us by H John Benjamin and Maeve Higgins

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
They're made out of meat.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Meat?

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Meat -- they're made out of meat

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Meat.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
There's no doubt about it. We picked several from different parts of the planet and we took them aboard our recon vessels

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
probed them -- all the way through! They're completely meat.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
That's impossible what about the radio signals, the messages to the stars?

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Well, they use the radio waves to talk but the signals don't come from them

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The signals come from machines.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
So who made the machines? That's who we want to contact.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
They made the machines, that's what I'm trying to tell you. Meat made the machines.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
That's ridiculous. How can meat make a machine? You're asking me to believe in sentient meat?

14
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:03,000
I'm not asking you, I'm telling you. These creatures are the only sentient race in the sector, and they're made out of meat.

15
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Maybe they're like the Orpheli -- you know, a Carbon-based intelligence that goes through a meat stage.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Nope. They're born meat, and they die meat. We studied them for several of their lifespans -- which didn't take too long, do you have any idea the lifespan of meat?

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Spare me. Okay, maybe they're only part meat, you know, like the Weddeli -- a meat head with an electron plasma brain inside.

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:36,000
No, we thought of that since they do have meat heads like the Weddeli but I told you we probed them. They're meat, all the way through.

19
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,000
No brain?

20
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Oh there's a brain all right, it's just that the brain is made out of meat

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
So what does the thinking?

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
You're not understanding are you? The brain does the thinking -- the, the meat

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Thinking meat! You're asking me to believe in thinking meat?!

24
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Yes! Thinking meat, conscious meat, loving meat, dreaming meat... the meat is the whole deal! Are you getting the picture?

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Oh my God you're serious then. They're made out of meat.

26
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Finally! Yes, they are indeed made out of meat and they've been trying to get in touch with us for almost a hundred of their years.

27
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,000
So what does the meat have in mind?

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:34,000
First it wants to talk to us. Then I imagine it wants to explore the universe, contact other sentients, swap ideas and information, the usual.

29
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
We're supposed to talk to meat?

30
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
That's the idea. That's the message they're sending out by radio.

31
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
"Hello anyone out there? Anybody home?" That sort of thing.

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
They actually do talk, then? They use words, ideas, concepts?

33
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Oh yes, except they do it with meat.

34
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:59,000
I -- I thought you just told me that they used radio

35
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:06,000
They do, but what you think is on the radio? Meat sounds! You know how when you slap or flap meat it makes a noise?

36
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:13,000
They talk by flapping their meat at each other. They can even sing by squirting air through their meat!

37
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Oh my God singing meat this is all together too much. Um ... so what do you advise?

38
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Officially or unofficially?

39
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Both?

40
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Officially, we're required to contact welcome and log in any and all sentient races or multi-beings in the quadrant without prejudice fear or favor

41
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Now unofficially -- ugh! -- I advise we erase the records and just forget the whole thing.

42
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
I was hoping you would say that.

43
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:57,000
It seems harsh, but there is a limit. Do we really want to make contact with meat?

44
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:02,000
I agree 100%. What's there to say? "Hello meat, how's it going?"

45
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:08,000
But will this work? How many planets are we dealing with here?

46
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:13,000
 Oh just one. They can travel to other planets in special meat containers but they can't live in them,

47
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:21,000
 and being meat they only travel through C-space which limits them to the speed of light and it makes the possibility of their ever making contact pretty slim.

48
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Infinitesimal, in fact.

49
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:28,000
So we just pretend there's no one home in the universe?

50
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:34,000
That's it. Cruel. But you said it yourself. Who wants to meet meat?

51
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:39,000
And the ones who have been aboard our vessels, the ones you've probed -- you're sure they won't remember?

52
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
They'll be considered crackpots if they do. We went into their heads and smoothed out their meat so we're just a dream to them.

53
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:51,000
A dream to meat. How strangely appropriate that we should be meat's dream.

54
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
And we can mark this sector unoccupied.

55
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Good. Agreed. Officially and unofficially. Case Closed. Any others? Anyone interesting on that side of the Galaxy?

56
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Yes, a rather shy but sweet hydrogen core cluster intelligence in a class 9 star in g445 zone

57
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Was in contact two galactic rotations ago. Wants to be friendly again.

58
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
They always come around.

59
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:27,000
And why not? Imagine how unbearably how unutterably cold the universe would be if one were all alone

60
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:35,000
[Music]

61
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:43,000
